> With this implementation, `./?.lua;` will still not be added back correctly to threads when in `-l` mode, like in #40610. At least `package.path` is only being set in one place with this solution, so it is less janky then my impl.

what about setting, on `executor.c`

```
static bool nlua_is_lua_script = false;

  void nlua_init(char **argv, int argc, int lua_arg0)
  {
    nlua_is_lua_script = lua_arg0 > 0;
```

and on `nlua_common_vim_init()`

```
  lua_pushboolean(lstate, nlua_is_lua_script);
  lua_setfield(lstate, -2, "_is_lua_script");
```

then call it from `_init_packages.lua`
